{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/811497-lunar-3e-conversion-anima-banners","id":811497,"title":"Lunar 3e conversion: Anima banners","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-18T20:11:05-08:00","id":811497,"title":"Lunar 3e conversion: Anima banners","content":"So I've been working, on and off, on a Lunar conversion (as between 2 games our group has 4 Lunars). It's about half-finished, and I posted up some what I'd done before, but I think people were still absorbing the backer pdf. Also, it was very much tl;dr.<br /> <br /> So, I thought I'd try posting in short chunks to get more feedback.<br /> <br /> So first, as it's short and easy to argue about, here's what I have for the anima banners. Tell me what you think!<br /> <br /> A couple of notes: First, there's the always contraversial Changing Moon anima. On the one hand, it's really good and makes people think &quot;why am I not a Changing Moon?&quot; On the other hand, it's iconic enough that I don't really want to abandon it. So essentially I just weakened it and made their other powers weaker than the ones the other castes get.<br /> Second, there's the No Moons. I wanted to make playing a non-sorcerer No Moon just as good as a sorcerer No Moon. So took away their sorcery effect, and gave them a bonus to dealing with spirits instad, to fulfill their role as Shamans. But giving the mental Lunars a bonus on social rolls feels weird. Any suggestions are welcome.<br /> <br /> (Oh, also, for character gen, the idea is that Lunars choose 2 caste abilities from the list, and then 2 favoured abilities. I considered having them choose 3 of 4 caste attributes, like Solars choose 5 out of 8, but it was difficult to decide what they should have.)<br /> <br /> Also... do bonuses from anima banners count as bonuses from charms? I'd assume they don't, but someone on these forums said they do. That'd affect the balance.<br /> <u><b>Full Moons:</b></u><br /> <b>Caste Attributes: Strength, Dexterity, Stamina.</b><br /> <b>Anima Banner: </b><br /> For 5 motes, the Lunar may add half her essence (rounded up) in dice to all movement pools and feats of strength (both the dice pool and the minimum strength for particular feats) for one scene. At bonfire/iconic level, this ability is activated automatically at no cost.<br /> Once per scene, when the Full Moon is at bonfire or iconic anima display, she may add half her Essence score (rounded up) to her base Initiative upon resetting to base after a successful decisive attack.<br /> For 5 motes, the Full Moon may reset one Strength, Dexterity or Stamina charm with an outstanding reset condition. This ability can only be used once per day, and is reset when the moon rises in the evening. If this ability is used on a night of the Full Moon, <i>all </i>Strength, Dexterity and Stamina charms with outstanding reset conditions are reset.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Changing Moon: </b></u><br /> <b>Caste Attributes: Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance</b><br /> <b>Anima Banner: </b><br /> For 5 motes, the Changing Moon adds half her essence (rounded up) to her Guile and the difficulty to spot her tell for a scene. If her anima reaches the burning/iconic level, she gets this bonus automatically, as she is surrounded by an ever-shifting aura of light and shadows, concealing her identity. This also requires watchers her to make a Perception+Awareness roll, difficulty of her Essence, to identify her.<br /> As a simple action costing 5 motes, the Lunar can change the physical appearance of her true human form. She can change her height and weight by up to 50%, half or double her apparent age, and also change her facial features, ethnicity, colouration, and other minor physical features. She can also change her voice. No roll is required to look different, but if she attempts to take a form specific enough to impersonate a particular person, she must make a disguise roll as normal, though ignoring all penalties for a different ethnicity and body shape, and with a dice bonus equal to her Essence or 3, whichever is higher. If she knows the charm Twin-Faced Hero she can ignore the penalty for gender, and if she has the charm Hybrid Body Rearrangement and an appropriate animal form (such as a lion for a lion-man, a wolf for a wolf-girl, etc), she can roll to disguise herself as a beastman with no penalty.<br /> For 5 motes, the Changing Moon may reset one Charisma, Manipulation or Appearance charm with an outstanding reset condition. This ability can only be used once per day, and is reset when the moon rises in the evening.<br /> <br /> <u><b>No Moon:</b></u><br /> <b>Caste Attributes: Perception, Intelligence, Wits</b><br /> <b>Anima Banner: </b><br /> No Moons are master shamans, in tune with the worlds of spirit and nature. But more than that, they are steeped in forbidden knowledge and the dark secrets of the Witching Moon, making them adept at negotiating with spirits both holy and unholy. For 5 motes, for one scene all social influence attempts by the No Moon against gods, elementals, Fair Folk and demons gain (Essence or 5, whichever is lower) extra dice. In addition, the No Moon's Resolve is raised by (half her Essence rounded up, or 3, whichever is lower) against their social influence and charms. Note that this ability does not apply to ghosts; even Luna fears to learn the secrets of the dead Titans.<br /> As the Lunars who are aligned with the darkest of nights, No Moons can wrap themselves in shadow. For 3 motes, they can get (Essence or 3, whichever is higher) additional dice on a stealth attempt in shadow, darkness, or dim light.<br /> For 5 motes, the No Moon may reset one Perception, Intelligence or Wits charm with an outstanding reset condition. This ability can only be used once per day, and is reset when the moon rises in the evening. If this ability is used on a night of the New Moon, <i>all </i>Perception, Intelligence and Wits charms with outstanding reset conditions are reset.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T01:07:24-08:00","id":811600,"title":"","content":"Making one Caste better at shapeshifting than the others in any way would be like making one Aspect of Dragon-Blooded better at elemental conjuration than the other Aspects.<br /> <br /> If Full Moons get bonuses to physical tasks without shapeshifting, why not give Changing Moons bonuses to social tasks? You start with something good regarding Guile, why not continue in that vein with bonuses to Threaten and Inspire actions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T01:21:43-08:00","id":811604,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your advice!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/811497-lunar-3e-conversion-anima-banners?p=811600#post811600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Making one Caste better at shapeshifting than the others in any way would be like making one Aspect of Dragon-Blooded better at elemental conjuration than the other Aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is kind of an issue, yes. On the other hand, I don't want to say to two of my players &quot;nope, your characters suddenly can't use one of their most important shapeshifting powers that you use all the time&quot;.<br /> I'm wondering about making it an Appearance charm so anyone can potentially take it (but Changing Moons are most likely to, as it's probably favoured). Probably with the charm for changing your hair and stuff as the prerequisite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Full Moons get bonuses to physical tasks without shapeshifting, why not give Changing Moons bonuses to social tasks? You start with something good regarding Guile, why not continue in that vein with bonuses to Threaten and Inspire actions? </div> </div> </div>Like Solars, the castes ought to have powers that are useful for them. But I'm a bit hesitant to just say &quot;you get bonuses to the stats you use most&quot; because that's what, well, better stats are for. Or excellencies.<br /> Like how Zeniths get 3 powers that are useful for them, but don't just get &quot;moar dice&quot;. Actually, the only people who do get &quot;moar dice&quot; really are Dawns, and they don't get it to attack rolls.<br /> So, raising the difficulty of the Tell definitely works (not like you can raise it with excellencies), but I was a little hesitant with the Guile. Still, I decided in the end to go for it to big up their role as Tricksters. If anyone has an idea for another ability that'd be useful for tricksters that isn't just a bonus, I'd be interested in hearing it. (For the same reason, I'm unsure of the dice bonus that No Moons get on stealth, but I think that's marginal enough that it's fine).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:47:46-08:00","id":812076,"title":"","content":"I like it. My only real complaints are the same as Sunder's. I definitely prefer the idea of making the minor shapeshift an Appearance charm. I would even fold the stuff about hair-changing into it, rather than making it a pre-req.<br /> <br /> One other suggestion; since Solars have eight caste abilities and pick five, I think Lunars should probably be able to pick three of five caste attributes. Just off-hand, I'd add one of each other category for them; Charisma and Perception for Full Moons, Dexterity and Wits for Changing Moons, and Stamina and Manipulation for No Moons (who should probably be called New Moons, but that ship has sailed for 3e, I'm sure).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:51:37-08:00","id":812082,"title":"","content":"I don't really like them having &quot;Dawn reset but worse&quot; as a thing, it reminds me of Silver Solars too much :/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:55:52-08:00","id":812089,"title":"","content":"I tend to feel like the Full Moon's reset trick is 'Like A Dawn, But Worse'. Maybe have it be, like, they automatically reset everything at moonrise <i>and moonset</i>? Something that isn't obviously a nerfed copy. Or forget charm resets entirely and go with some kind of soak or regen trick that's not 'permitted' under the charmset.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ahahahaha Sidereal'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:55:22-08:00","id":812281,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your comments, this is very useful!<br /> <br /> With the resets, I wanted to give them a power that could be useful for a wide range of concepts, and not just combat. They're physical exalts, rather than just combat exalts. Similarly for No Moons. But I thought resetting all physical charms would be better than resetting combat charms. Thinking about it though, maybe it actually isn't? Or at least, not significantly? Also, obviously, I was trying to give them all 3 powers and that's what I thought of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think any soak or regen is going to feel like a charm, but maybe I could do something with regen...<br /> <br /> Okay, so if I take away Changing Moon's shapeshifting and make it a charm, what to have instead?<br /> <br /> Finally, what do people think of the No Moon's shaman ability? Feels weird to give No Moons a social ability, but I feel they should do something shamanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-19-2016, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T18:59:10-08:00","id":812283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WarDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/811497-lunar-3e-conversion-anima-banners?p=812076#post812076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like it. My only real complaints are the same as Sunder's. I definitely prefer the idea of making the minor shapeshift an Appearance charm. I would even fold the stuff about hair-changing into it, rather than making it a pre-req.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think as it's 3rd ed, and that's a really good ability, it should probably be over 2 charms. I'll write them up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One other suggestion; since Solars have eight caste abilities and pick five, I think Lunars should probably be able to pick three of five caste attributes. Just off-hand, I'd add one of each other category for them; Charisma and Perception for Full Moons, Dexterity and Wits for Changing Moons, and Stamina and Manipulation for No Moons (who should probably be called New Moons, but that ship has sailed for 3e, I'm sure). </div> </div> </div>Could do I guess (though I'd want to give Full Moons Appearance... and why Stamina for No Moons?).<br /> <br /> But the other thing I was thinking of is tattooing. See, you've got your casteless Lunar with 4 favoured attributes (giving them 3, then an extra one when they exalt, is a bit awkward). 2 of them are going to be in the same attribute, and thus obviously they're from that caste and the other two are favoured attributes. For example, if they have Dex, Stamina, Charisma and Wits, then they're a Full Moon. But if you have them choose 3 caste attrbutes and 1 favoured attribute, the Casteless with his 4 favoured attributes might just not &quot;fit&quot; the 3 caste attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:42:13-08:00","id":812313,"title":"","content":"I... really can't agree that just changing the color and style of your hair should be its own Charm. Even if clothes are thrown in. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Appearance works for Full Moons as well. I picked Stamina mostly because shamans have to endure a lot of hardships for their calling, and it made more sense than Strength or dexterity.<br /> <br /> In the case of tattooing a casteless, well, that just sucks for him. He'd lose one of his favored attributes, and either just buy the new attribute as favored and carry on (if the ST wants to be generous) or recalculate all his charm costs and likely go into debt (if being ungenerous).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:48:38-08:00","id":812321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/811497-lunar-3e-conversion-anima-banners?p=812281#post812281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for your comments, this is very useful!<br /> <br /> With the resets, I wanted to give them a power that could be useful for a wide range of concepts, and not just combat. They're physical exalts, rather than just combat exalts. Similarly for No Moons. But I thought resetting all physical charms would be better than resetting combat charms. Thinking about it though, maybe it actually isn't? Or at least, not significantly? Also, obviously, I was trying to give them all 3 powers and that's what I thought of. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the thing that I was keying off of was that the Dawn Anima resets <i>all</i> Combat Charm Timers, right? Only letting Full Moons reset <i>one single </i>charm is weaksauce in comparison, even if it's not limited to a particular class of charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}